    "user_prompt": "Build an 8-bit dual-stream join datapath as a complete SR2FPGA Verilog RTL project. This is component topology t4_dual_stream_join, difficulty tier T4. Use two skid_buffer instances feeding stream_join, then accumulator_core, then stream_stage. The design must implement this black-box behavior: two valid-ready input streams are buffered, synchronized, joined, accumulated, and staged. Keep rtl/top.v as the integration wrapper and keep each reusable component in a separate RTL file. Preserve these interface contracts: top.in0_valid -> skid_buffer.in_valid; top.in0_data -> skid_buffer.in_data; top.in1_valid -> skid_buffer.in_valid; top.in1_data -> skid_buffer.in_data; skid_buffer.out_valid -> stream_join.in0_valid; skid_buffer.out_data -> stream_join.in0_data; skid_buffer.out_valid -> stream_join.in1_valid; skid_buffer.out_data -> stream_join.in1_data; stream_join.in0_ready -> skid_buffer.out_ready; stream_join.in1_ready -> skid_buffer.out_ready; stream_join.out_valid -> accumulator_core.sample_valid; stream_join.out_data -> accumulator_core.sample; stream_stage.in_ready -> stream_join.out_ready; accumulator_core.sample_valid -> stream_stage.in_valid; accumulator_core.sum -> stream_stage.in_data; stream_stage.in_ready -> accumulator_core.sample_ready; top.out_ready -> stream_stage.out_ready; stream_stage.out_valid -> top.out_valid; stream_stage.out_data -> top.out_data. Include system_his.json, manifest.json, timing constraints, predicted QoR, and a bounded self-checking testbench that prints TEST_PASS only on success or TEST_FAIL on failure.",
    "design_goal": "Implement an 8-bit dual-stream join datapath using skid_buffer, stream_join, accumulator_core, and stream_stage instances.",
